{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the earth was corrupted before Elohim, etc.</b> 'Elohim' means the judges, for they would steal less than a perutah's worth, concerning which the courts do not issue a claim, and the judge's eyes see yet he has no power to save the tears of the oppressed. Therefore it says 'before the Elohim' — literally before them. And for this reason 'the earth was filled with violence.' And a support for this is from what we find in the Yalkut on Psalms: 'אַשְׁרֵי הָאִישׁ' — this is Noah, etc.; 'עַל כֵּן לֹא יָקֻמוּ רְשָׁעִים בַּמִּשְׁפָּט' — this is the generation of the Flood. What does it mean that this verse speaks of the generation of the Flood? And it appears that he based it on the beginning of the matter: 'לֹא כֵן הָרְשָׁעִים כִּי אִם כַּמֹּץ אֲשֶׁר תִּדְּפֶנּוּ רוּחַ' (Psalms 1:4) — that is, 'לֹא כֵן' means they were not honest and truthful in their deeds, for they schemed to steal little by little like this chaff that is not worth a perutah, 'אֲשֶׁר תִּדְּפֶנּוּ רוּחַ' — the judges in whom the spirit of HaShem dwells. 'עַל כֵּן לֹא יָקֻמוּ רְשָׁעִים בַּמִּשְׁפָּט' (Psalms 1:5), for it was not in their power to bring them to justice, for the judge does not attend to less than a perutah's worth. And for this reason, even the sinner who stood in the assembly of the righteous and said, 'I am righteous like you' — this is what it says: 'וְחַטָּאִים בַּעֲדַת צַדִּיקִים' (Psalms 1:5), for both of them had the audacity to say, 'I am like you.' And if they concealed their wickedness from people, nevertheless before the Holy One, blessed be He, it was known who was the righteous one and who was the wicked one — this is what it says: 'כִּי יוֹדֵעַ ה׳ דֶּרֶךְ צַדִּיקִים וְדֶרֶךְ רְשָׁעִים תֹּאבֵד' (Psalms 1:6)."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:23.652509269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}